<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.bibbi88.HydGineer</id>
  <name>HydGineer</name>
  <summary>Draw and simulate hydraulic circuits</summary>
  <developer id="io.github.bibbi88">
    <name>bibbi88</name>
  </developer>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.bibbi88.HydGineer.desktop</launchable>
  <description>
    <p>
      HydGineer is a hydraulic circuit editor and simulator for learning and teaching hydraulics
      and electro-hydraulics. Drag pumps, valves, cylinders and motors onto a canvas, wire them
      together with ISO 1219 symbols and run the simulation: every line shows its pressure and
      flow, solved from the actual hydraulic relationships.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Directional, pressure and flow control valves, load sensing, steering units and more</li>
      <li>Cylinders and motors with loads, friction or efficiency, and moving masses</li>
      <li>Electrical control: push buttons, relays, solenoids, sensors and a small PLC</li>
      <li>Ready-made example circuits to start from</li>
      <li>Several circuits open at once, in tabs</li>
      <li>Export to PDF, PNG and SVG, one circuit or many</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The simulation is a simplified model for education. It is not a design or safety tool.
    </p>
  </description>
